  "rationale": "The requirement has one obligation. The getting-started documentation MUST explain that the session-start hook tells the agent to load the `habeas` skill.\n\nTwo tests in `tests/repository.rs` cover it. Both carry `{test}` references to the subject. Both check `README.md` and `md/getting_started.md`, the only getting-started documents I found.\n\n- `getting_started_documents_symposium_setup_and_skill_migration` asserts that both files contain \"session\", \"hook\" and \"`habeas` skill\". It also asserts that a single whitespace-normalized paragraph contains \"hook tells\", \"load the `habeas` skill before starting any work\" and \"session\". That ties the skill-loading instruction to the hook in one paragraph.\n- `installation_guides_cover_setup_hooks_refresh_and_preserving_local_skills` asserts that both files contain \"load the `habeas` skill\" and \"advises the agent\". It asserts the exact `README.md` sentence: \"Its session-start hook tells the agent that the project tracks requirements with Habeas and to load the `habeas` skill before starting any work.\" It asserts the exact `md/getting_started.md` sentence: \"When an agent starts a session in this project, Habeas's hook tells it that the project tracks requirements with Habeas and to load the `habeas` skill before starting any work.\"\n\nThe search results show the guide sentence in `md/getting_started.md` and the `README.md` sentence in the docs. The assertions are specific enough that removing or changing the explanation would fail them. No other obligations, boundaries or modes apply. The documentation is a text artifact, so the string assertions are the appropriate check. No gaps found.",
